The selected CPython release and its derived ABI version are defined once in
projects/versions.mk. The bundled pip wheel version used for Android packaging
is also declared there so a CPython update cannot silently select a different
wheel in a build rule.

Building:
- configure scripts need explicit build and target environments
  (--build, --host, and --with-build-python)
- PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR needs to be exported so that it is visible in processes
  spawned by the configure script
- Android Python depends on the project-built OpenSSL libraries so `_ssl` and
  `_hashlib` are available.
- Cross-compiled `ensurepip` cannot execute the Android interpreter on the
  build host. Instead, the matching wheel already bundled by CPython is
  installed directly into the Android `site-packages` tree.
